msgid "freeports\\_dev.classification\\_check"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.classification_check:1 of
msgid ""
"The document-classification test of a formats repository: is each test "
"report recognised as the format whose folder it sits in?"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.classification_check:4 of
msgid ""
"Phase 13 of ``agent-memory/PLAN-document-classification.md``. One test "
"per document (:class:`freeports_dev.pytest_plugin.ReportVariant`), named "
"``test_classification``. It passes when the engine classifies the "
"document as the folder's format, or does not classify it at all, or stops"
" at a partial that the folder's format refines; it fails when the "
"document is classified as another format, when a partial excludes the "
"folder's format, and when the classifier errs."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.classification_check:10 of
msgid ""
"The engine is asked through ``freeports classify`` (one subprocess per "
"document) and its default one-line-per-document output is parsed: there "
"is no Python entry point for document classification, and adding one is "
"not this package's call."
msgstr ""

